<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto 34px">
      <span class="eyebrow reveal">How the work runs</span>
      <h2 class="reveal d1">Three visits, not one</h2>
      <p class="lead center reveal d2">A single clean at the end never holds. Dust keeps falling while the last trades finish, so we come back.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-auto">
      <div class="feat ac-navy reveal"><span class="ptag tg-blue">Visit 1</span><h3>Rough clean</h3><p>Once the trades are off site we clear debris and bulk dust, working top down. Ceilings, walls, ledges, window tracks, then floors.</p></div>
      <div class="feat ac-orange reveal d1"><span class="ptag tg-sky">Visit 2</span><h3>Detail clean</h3><p>After the dust has settled we wipe fixtures, doors, frames and skirting, clean glass, sanitary ware and kitchens, then finish the floors.</p></div>
      <div class="feat ac-blue reveal d2"><span class="ptag tg-gold">Visit 3</span><h3>Handover clean</h3><p>Shortly before inspection we return for horizontal surfaces, vents, glass and any marks the follow-on trades have left.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead center reveal d2" style="margin-top:28px">Your team is paid to build. Cleaning pulls skilled labour off the programme at the point where delay costs most, and a snagging list that includes dust is a snagging list that holds up payment.</p>
  </div>
</section>

